{"key":"34576f59a829a070","source_file":"Potts Ca - Ce.json","source_id":10491,"source_url":"concordance-carbuncle-ppl-carbunculus","term":"Carbuncle","headwords":["Carbuncle"],"latin":["Carbunculus"],"header_pairs":[{"english":["Carbuncle"],"latin":["Carbunculus"]}],"header_sentences":[],"redirect_xref":null,"works":["AC","AE"],"contexts":[{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"9865","subsection":null},"text":"A ruby, a topaz, a carbuncle () = the celestial love of good... The reason these stones = this love, is their red and flaming colour.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"9865","subsection":"end"},"text":"Carbuncle, in the Original Language, is derived from a word which means flashing, as from fire.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AE","section":"401","subsection":"25"},"text":"Carbuncles () = their resplendence from good.","comment":null,"footnote":null}],"slug":"carbuncle-34576f","url":"/meta/potts/carbuncle-34576f/"}